  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian Capacity Building and Partners Accompanier Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The quality of CAFOD&#x2019;s work is reflected by the quality of work done by its local partners. This project is about capacity building focused on improving the quality of work and accountability of partners. It will also seeks to help partners to improve their administrative systems and procedures in areas such as human resources, finance, supply chain and logistics, parish and diocesan project implementation and administration guidelines. The outcomes will be improved effectiveness in delivery of humanitarian and development work and improved accountability of partners and administrative systems. 

Emphasis will be on key aspects of humanitarian work, better implementation of emergency responses including improving community managed disaster risk reduction and preparedness. Training activities will be on project cycle management, managing emergency response, international humanitarian principles and  humanitarian standards such as Good Enough Guide, HAP-I, Sphere, LEGS (for partners that deal with pastoral communities) Red Cross Code of Conduct and so on. The project will build the partners confidence and and consistence in applying international humanitarian standards and principles in their programming. Whilst some capacity exists in the partners this project seeks to strengthen the capacity of the partners to respond to emergency situations and to mitigate the impact of humanitarian disasters in their areas of operation.

A Programme Accompanier shall be recruited who will work with CAFOD partners in Northern Kenya to provide technical support for capacity building and projects management. The Programme Accompanier shall provide technical support to three northern Kenya Catholic dioceses (Marsabit, Maralal and Isiolo) in planning, capacity building and implementation of humanitarian programmes and coordination. The accompanier will encourage joint planning and learning by the partners including ensuring adoption of good practices. The Programme accompanier will be an employee of CAFOD but will operate from the Diocese of Isiolo Offices in Isiolo town.</narrative>
  </description>
